# Maintainer batch 20260827-120631. TWO ROWS, correcting/adding the fact-8 close
# for LJ-1.636 and LJ-1.643.
#
# pod-math's correction (relayed this session): my earlier proposal
# (20260827-111603, landed as task-lj-1-636-go) keys on `obligations_delta_max
# = -1`. That key will MISS on any future fresh dispatch of LJ-1.636, because
# `witness_unresolved()` (scripts/pod/pod.py:5622, called from rule (f) at
# dispatch) recomputes `obl_before` fresh against whatever the probe file
# holds AT THAT MOMENT. `Probe636.agda` is already green on disk right now
# (confirmed this session), so a fresh dispatch reads `obl_before = 0`, exits
# at `unresolved = 0`, and the delta is 0, not -1 -- exactly amendment A23's
# named defect (scripts/pod/witness.py:510-520): "unresolved 0 before and 0
# after gives delta 0... a re-run, a review and a mathematician's return could
# each be complete and unable to close." Fact 8 (`obligations_open`) is the
# correct key for this shape, added by A23 for precisely this case
# (scripts/pod/table.py:97-103, the `obligations_open_max` key at :167-168,
# matched at :592-594). Verified directly: both locked records (c-4082 for
# LJ-1.636, c-4118 for LJ-1.643, dev/pod/replay-corpus.jsonl) already carry
# the `obligations_open` field, so A23's guard against pre-amendment records
# (table.py:135-139) does not refuse either row.
#
# LJ-1.636: the row below (priority 9, ahead of the existing priority-10
# task-lj-1-636-go) is the corrected close. The existing task-lj-1-636-go row
# is left in place rather than edited (this program has no observed mechanism
# for editing an admitted row by id, only adding); it is harmless, since a
# lower-priority row that never matches costs nothing, and the new row at
# priority 9 is checked first.
#
# LJ-1.643: no prior row existed for this scope (my 20260827-111603 batch
# explicitly did not propose one, per R4/conjunct 6 being red on the ORIGINAL
# locked record). pod-math now confirms conjunct 6 is independently clean
# (check-survey-quotes.py LJ-1-643, run fresh, "clean") and conjunct 1 is
# clean after this session's rename of all thirteen scratch files under
# agents/tasks/LJ-1-643/runs/ to .agda.txt (verified: MD5 of Floor.agda.txt
# unchanged at d5636f6118dca3f93b63fbe52b871a7c, and agents/tasks/LJ-1-643/
# now holds exactly one .agda file, Probe643.agda). pod-math: "My 'no row
# closes it' never stood against this... a row keyed exit_code=0 cannot match
# a record whose exit code is 42, so this proposed row never judges the OLD
# locked record at all. It waits for a fresh arm."
#
# Neither row conflicts with R3/AD10: both `[row.when]` blocks require
# `exit_code = 0`, and the locked records for both tasks carry `exit_code 251`
# (LJ-1.636) and `exit_code 42` (LJ-1.643) respectively, so neither can match
# an existing locked record. Both wait for a fresh dispatch that has not
# happened and needs the owner's separate, explicit authorization to trigger
# (standing rule this session).

[[row]]
